    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21357" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ</span></b> , third letter in Gr. alphabet; as Numeral <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ́</span>
		=
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>three, third, thrice</i>:
			also, with pr. n., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βάσσος γ́</span>”
				<i>B., son and grandson of B.,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IGRom.
					4.1587
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc.: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				g'
			</span>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				000
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> written for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ</span>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γανδάνειν: ἀρέσκειν</span>,
			etc.</div>
